      "problem": "Evaluate the following matrix product:\n\n|  | $2$ | $0$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ |  |  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3$ | $-1$ | $4$ |  |  |  | $3$ | $0$ | $2$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} | $10$ | {{field-4}} |  |\n|  | $0$ | $2$ | $5$ |  |  |  | $2$ | $1$ | $3$ |  |  |  | $16$ | {{field-5}} | $19$ |  |",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying each row in the first matrix by each column in the second, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+0+2 & 4+0+1 & 2+0+3 \\\\ 3-3+8 & 6+0+4 & 3-2+12 \\\\ 0+6+10 & 0+0+5 & 0+4+15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 10 & 13 \\\\ 16 & 5 & 19\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
